---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About ScamPrep: Who Built It and Why"
  description="Why we're pointing the proven simulated-training playbook at the people scammers target most, with consent, dignity, and proof."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>Why we're building ScamPrep.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        In 2025, Americans over 60 reported more losses to scams than ever before:
      </p>
      <ul class="stat-bullets">
        <li><strong>$7.7 billion</strong> reported lost, up <strong>59%</strong> in a single year</li>
        <li><strong>More than 200,000</strong> complaints filed with the FBI</li>
        <li><strong>$38,000</strong> lost by the average victim, enough to erase years of savings</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Behind every one of those numbers is a family, and often a retirement, changed by a
        single phone call or text.
      </p>
      <p>
        What struck us was the mismatch.
        <strong>If you've ever received a fake "phishing test" email at work, you've already had
        scam training that works.</strong> For more than a decade, virtually every major
        company, bank, and government agency has drilled its people against these exact tactics
        with simulated attacks and in-the-moment coaching. It's a proven playbook with years of
        evidence behind it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Meanwhile, the standard offering for the people scammers actually target most is a
        pamphlet and a one-time seminar whose effect, research shows, fades within a month.
      </p>
      <p>
        ScamPrep exists to close that gap: to take the most effective training method we know of
        and finally point it at the people who need it, with the consent, gentleness, and dignity
        that training someone you love demands.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <!-- Photo + bio: image left, text right; stacks photo-first on mobile. -->
      <div class="founder">
        <img
          class="founder__photo"
          src="/bryce-wachtell.jpg"
          alt="Bryce Wachtell, founder of ScamPrep"
          width="800"
          height="800"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <div class="founder__bio prose">
          <h2>The founder</h2>
          <p>
            ScamPrep is built by <strong>Bryce Wachtell</strong>. Bryce spent his career in strategy
            and operations at Google, as a management consultant at Bain &amp; Company, and at an
            early-stage startup called Gatheround. He turned down business school at Stanford
            University to build ScamPrep after observing the growing threat of scams in his own
            community. He builds the way he believes protective products should be built: simple,
            elegant, research-backed, and unambiguously good for the people they serve.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can connect with Bryce
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/j-bryce-wachtell/">on LinkedIn</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Our principles</h2>
        <p class="lede">Four commitments we hold ourselves to, in every drill, briefing, and report.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top: 32px;">
        <div class="card principle">
          <h3>Independence, not surveillance</h3>
          <p>
            We don't watch bank accounts or monitor anyone's life. ScamPrep builds the skill that
            lets people keep confidently handling their own affairs. Empowerment over oversight.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card principle">
          <h3>Research-built</h3>
          <p>
            Every drill and briefing traces back to published research and to the scams currently
            being reported to the FBI and FTC. When the evidence changes, the product changes.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card principle">
          <h3>Proof over promises</h3>
          <p>
            No training can guarantee protection, so we never claim it. Instead we show families
            measurable progress every quarter, and we make refunds easy when we haven't earned our
            keep.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card principle">
          <h3>Dignity first, consent always</h3>
          <p>
            We coach, we never shame. Nobody receives a drill who hasn't personally said yes, and
            nothing happens behind anyone's back.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="prose" style="margin-top: 36px;">
        We're in early access and building with our founding families and partners. Want to shape
        it? <a href="/early-access">Get early access</a> or write us at
        <a href="mailto:hello@getscamprep.com">hello@getscamprep.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>

<style>
  .stat-bullets {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.2em;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .stat-bullets li {
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--ink);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 12px 18px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }
  .stat-bullets strong { color: var(--pine-deep); }
  /* Founder: photo + bio. Card radius and hairline border match the system;
     the studio-gray photo background sits naturally on the paper section. */
  .founder {
    display: grid;
    gap: 28px;
    align-items: center;
    max-width: 56rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .founder { grid-template-columns: 260px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 44px; }
  }
  .founder__photo {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 260px;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .founder__bio h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .founder__bio p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .principle h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .principle p { margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.55; }
</style>
